 },
 "d24621070790": {
  "file": "d24621070790.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 4.39,
  "bytes": 26589,
  "text": "It has to be in your handwriting. Terrible is fine. Take your time."
 },
 "228467b00ce0": {
  "file": "228467b00ce0.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 3.22,
  "bytes": 19533,
  "text": "Bob, your city and zip are still blank. Could you add them?"
 },
 "7f964cab7634": {
  "file": "7f964cab7634.mp3",
  "who": "bob",
  "voice": "el:CwhRBWXzGAHq8TQ4Fs17:0.88",
  "dur": 3.74,
  "bytes": 22701,
  "text": "It's Los Angeles, nine oh oh two four. There you go."
 },
 "dc8d6fa44c83": {
  "file": "dc8d6fa44c83.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 1.7,
  "bytes": 10461,
  "text": "That's a good line. Thank you!"
 },
 "25845b44eb1b": {
  "file": "25845b44eb1b.mp3",
  "who": "bob",
  "voice": "el:CwhRBWXzGAHq8TQ4Fs17:0.88",
  "dur": 1.3,
  "bytes": 8013,
  "text": "Thank you! Good luck."
 },
 "e9bac44932d5": {
  "file": "e9bac44932d5.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 9.38,
  "bytes": 56541,
  "text": "The signer writes every word, so the pen stays in his hand. And one look before he leaves catches a gap while it can still be fixed."
 },
 "d1c2f880ad8c": {
  "file": "d1c2f880ad8c.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 7.13,
  "bytes": 43005,
  "text": "Now it's your turn to look at four lines. Tap the box that will get each line thrown out, or tap Good to go."
 },
 "434227eb00cf": {
  "file": "434227eb00cf.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 9.17,
  "bytes": 55245,
  "text": "C is right. Never use white-out, and never write on a signer's line. A fresh line in the signer's own writing is the fix."
 },
 "3ea2bb80a82e": {
  "file": "3ea2bb80a82e.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 14.28,
  "bytes": 85917,
  "text": "C is right. His line needs his current address, and it must match his voter record. He can update his registration at register to vote dot C A dot gov, then sign. Never promise his line will count."
 },
 "27bc6cc8939c": {
  "file": "27bc6cc8939c.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 12.79,
  "bytes": 76989,
  "text": "Every sheet has one more line, and it's yours: the Declaration of Circulator. It says you gathered these signatures, watched each one being written and showed every signer this month's top funders."
 },
 "1f965027929a": {
  "file": "1f965027929a.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 15.91,
  "bytes": 95709,
  "text": "The blank one and the one your lead filled in each cost the whole sheet. After the last signature, write your name, your address and the first and last days you gathered on that sheet. Then sign and date it, all in your own writing."
 },
 "a23bfd78aeaf": {
  "file": "a23bfd78aeaf.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 9.07,
  "bytes": 54669,
  "text": "A woman with her daughter is registered and ready to sign. Before the pen moves, ask if she's signed this one already. Then walk her through the line."
 },
 "84ce22487481": {
  "file": "84ce22487481.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 4.46,
  "bytes": 27021,
  "text": "Can you fill in the address for me, though? I've got my hands full with this one."
 },
 "76102c937c9e": {
  "file": "76102c937c9e.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 3.98,
  "bytes": 24141,
  "text": "Can you fill in the address for me? I've got my hands full with this one.",
  "take": 2
 },
 "fc62dbf79798": {
  "file": "fc62dbf79798.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.97,
  "bytes": 12045,
  "text": "Okay, I'll write it. Hang on."
 },
 "f49ccec5a84a": {
  "file": "f49ccec5a84a.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 0.82,
  "bytes": 5133,
  "text": "All set?"
 },
 "eb763263f20e": {
  "file": "eb763263f20e.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.7,
  "bytes": 10461,
  "text": "Oh! I skipped it."
 },
 "a2c1035880d7": {
  "file": "a2c1035880d7.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 0.94,
  "bytes": 5853,
  "text": "There you go."
 },
 "3a40d6a2f1c3": {
  "file": "3a40d6a2f1c3.mp3",
  "who": "tanya",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.13,
  "bytes": 7005,
  "text": "Great, thanks!"
 },
 "845f9061ced8": {
  "file": "845f9061ced8.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 4.46,
  "bytes": 27021,
  "text": "The signer writes every word on their line, and that's a must. Try it once more."
 },
 "a6f832d0a1f1": {
  "file": "a6f832d0a1f1.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 6.19,
  "bytes": 37389,
  "text": "Let's try one. An older man stopped, and you told him what the measure does. He has a question for you."
 },
 "12419f032e5b": {
  "file": "12419f032e5b.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 2.21,
  "bytes": 13485,
  "text": "Hold on. Is this a new tax?"
 },
 "846dbf506f60": {
  "file": "846dbf506f60.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 5.16,
  "bytes": 31197,
  "text": "Huh. Okay. At least you told me straight. I'll sign."
 },
 "cadf109c2db5": {
  "file": "cadf109c2db5.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 3.05,
  "bytes": 18525,
  "text": "Says here it's a tax. I'll pass, thanks."
 },
 "e4d9c12cca74": {
  "file": "e4d9c12cca74.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 0.48,
  "bytes": 3117,
  "text": "Hi."
 },
 "bf1caff193c3": {
  "file": "bf1caff193c3.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 1.2,
  "bytes": 7437,
  "text": "I'm good, thanks."
 },
 "abea03472814": {
  "file": "abea03472814.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 0.96,
  "bytes": 5997,
  "text": "I'll think about it."
 },
 "e1736ee5c7c8": {
  "file": "e1736ee5c7c8.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 1.49,
  "bytes": 9165,
  "text": "Okay, bye now."
 },
 "19f2e571f82d": {
  "file": "19f2e571f82d.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 2.35,
  "bytes": 14349,
  "text": "Sorry, I've got to run. Good luck!"
 },
 "074d3859b240": {
  "file": "074d3859b240.mp3",
  "who": "hank",
  "voice": "el:pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4:0.88",
  "dur": 1.61,
  "bytes": 9885,
  "text": "Thanks! Good luck out here."
 },
 "8ce9f21434c4": {
  "file": "8ce9f21434c4.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 5.26,
  "bytes": 31773,
  "text": "Listen to a trained canvasser answer a hard question. A woman has stopped at the table."
 },
 "9caca893320a": {
  "file": "9caca893320a.mp3",
  "who": "joan",
  "voice": "el:aIu5oHglU5AHNc2x0AZu:0.9",
  "dur": 1.85,
  "bytes": 11325,
  "text": "Is this going to raise taxes?"
 },
 "45654e06e703": {
  "file": "45654e06e703.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 10.25,
  "bytes": 61725,
  "text": "Yes. It's a new state tax on digital advertising sales. That's how it pays for the longer hours. It's printed right here in the summary. Take a look."
 },
 "727d121bc273": {
  "file": "727d121bc273.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 0.89,
  "bytes": 5565,
  "text": "Want to sign?"
 },
 "ad0946736069": {
  "file": "ad0946736069.mp3",
  "who": "joan",
  "voice": "el:aIu5oHglU5AHNc2x0AZu:0.9",
  "dur": 2.38,
  "bytes": 14493,
  "text": "No, not today. I buy a lot of ads."
 },
 "62ddb675147e": {
  "file": "62ddb675147e.mp3",
  "who": "lena",
  "voice": "el:cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9:0.88",
  "dur": 3.1,
  "bytes": 18813,
  "text": "No problem. Thanks for stopping. Have a good one."
 },
 "1e07816bce20": {
  "file": "1e07816bce20.mp3",
  "who": "joan",
  "voice": "el:aIu5oHglU5AHNc2x0AZu:0.9",
  "dur": 2.16,
  "bytes": 13197,
  "text": "You too. Thanks for being straight with me."
 },
 "a0f3a3cc5c66": {
  "file": "a0f3a3cc5c66.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 7.03,
  "bytes": 42429,
  "text": "Some people sign after a straight answer and some don't. Either way, she's free for the next person in twenty seconds."
 },
 "1df2ae6ab454": {
  "file": "1df2ae6ab454.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 4.58,
  "bytes": 27741,
  "text": "You'll hear these four questions this week. Tap the straight answer to each one."
 },
 "314b16e7e9e7": {
  "file": "314b16e7e9e7.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 3.91,
  "bytes": 23709,
  "text": "B is right. You already said you're paid once, so say it again."
 },
 "48a794d13ca0": {
  "file": "48a794d13ca0.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 5.21,
  "bytes": 31485,
  "text": "A is right. A signature helps put the question on the ballot, and it isn't a vote."
 },
 "46acc9b031fa": {
  "file": "46acc9b031fa.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 8.11,
  "bytes": 48909,
  "text": "B is right. Never guess. 'I don't know, but it's printed right here' is a whole answer, and you can ask your lead later."
 },
 "8569c3b22682": {
  "file": "8569c3b22682.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 6.43,
  "bytes": 38829,
  "text": "A is right. Giving anything of value for a signature is against the law, even something small."
 },
 "a682a6f113eb": {
  "file": "a682a6f113eb.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 4.9,
  "bytes": 29613,
  "text": "Here's the new canvasser one last time. Listen for the part that goes wrong."
 },
 "bab27c60d991": {
  "file": "bab27c60d991.mp3",
  "who": "karim",
  "voice": "el:pNInz6obpgDQGcFmaJgB:0.88",
  "dur": 1.46,
  "bytes": 9021,
  "text": "Is this a tax thing?"
 },
 "419a5b5eaca1": {
  "file": "419a5b5eaca1.mp3",
  "who": "rico",
  "voice": "el:bIHbv24MWmeRgasZH58o:0.88",
  "dur": 6.17,
  "bytes": 37245,
  "text": "Don't worry about that part. It's all about keeping libraries open later. It's right here. Want to sign?"
 },
 "de472af5ff98": {
  "file": "de472af5ff98.mp3",
  "who": "karim",
  "voice": "el:pNInz6obpgDQGcFmaJgB:0.88",
  "dur": 1.13,
  "bytes": 7005,
  "text": "No, I'll pass."
 },
 "4679d985eef9": {
  "file": "4679d985eef9.mp3",
  "who": "rico",
  "voice": "el:bIHbv24MWmeRgasZH58o:0.88",
  "dur": 1.63,
  "bytes": 10029,
  "text": "No problem. Have a good one.",
  "take": 3
 },
 "f01a8ae87179": {
  "file": "f01a8ae87179.mp3",
  "who": "karim",
  "voice": "el:pNInz6obpgDQGcFmaJgB:0.88",
  "dur": 1.37,
  "bytes": 8445,
  "text": "Thanks. You too."
 },
 "289af24b8d00": {
  "file": "289af24b8d00.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 5.54,
  "bytes": 33501,
  "text": "Your last try. A man with a coffee has stopped, and you've told him what the measure does."
 },
 "69c69903a217": {
  "file": "69c69903a217.mp3",
  "who": "ben",
  "voice": "el:cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal:0.88",
  "dur": 1.56,
  "bytes": 9597,
  "text": "Wait. Are you a volunteer?",
  "take": 2
 },
 "c7332173d537": {
  "file": "c7332173d537.mp3",
  "who": "ben",
  "voice": "el:cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal:0.88",
  "dur": 1.92,
  "bytes": 11757,
  "text": "Fair enough. Thanks for telling me."
 },
 "8f250d52f639": {
  "file": "8f250d52f639.mp3",
  "who": "ben",
  "voice": "el:cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal:0.88",
  "dur": 2.42,
  "bytes": 14781,
  "text": "Sorry, but are you a volunteer or not?",
  "take": 4
 },
 "af98d2cd11f0": {
  "file": "af98d2cd11f0.mp3",
  "who": "ben",
  "voice": "el:cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal:0.88",
  "dur": 2.54,
  "bytes": 15501,
  "text": "Okay. Is there something you want me to sign?",
  "take": 1
 },
 "ffc072aedcad": {
  "file": "ffc072aedcad.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 3.14,
  "bytes": 19101,
  "text": "Before I sign anything, is this a new tax?"
 },
 "0afd7a27c245": {
  "file": "0afd7a27c245.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.58,
  "bytes": 9741,
  "text": "So what do you want me to do?"
 },
 "276b0d49e447": {
  "file": "276b0d49e447.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 3.43,
  "bytes": 20829,
  "text": "That isn't what I asked. Is it a new tax or not?"
 },
 "48b19a77bc5d": {
  "file": "48b19a77bc5d.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.85,
  "bytes": 11325,
  "text": "I appreciate the straight answer."
 },
 "8f35f6fba9c3": {
  "file": "8f35f6fba9c3.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 3.17,
  "bytes": 19245,
  "text": "No. I don't sign anything with a new tax in it."
 },
 "4c619cc9ccbe": {
  "file": "4c619cc9ccbe.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 3.65,
  "bytes": 22125,
  "text": "You're the first one out here who just told me. Good luck."
 },
 "b903c33bf34a": {
  "file": "b903c33bf34a.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.34,
  "bytes": 8301,
  "text": "Okay. Bye now."
 },
 "c7371daba941": {
  "file": "c7371daba941.mp3",
  "who": "pat",
  "voice": "el:XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX:0.88",
  "dur": 1.63,
  "bytes": 10029,
  "text": "Like I said, no thanks."
 },
 "989d2e20eb9a": {
  "file": "989d2e20eb9a.mp3",
  "who": "coach",
  "voice": "el:bRlp5mUWs01wX4H4oW4X:0.9",
  "dur": 3.6,
  "bytes": 21837,
  "text": "A straight, true answer is a must. Try it once more."
 }
}
